    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d591">

                <pb facs="0635" n="531" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg531"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.001J56/10: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Eberhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-05-04T11:00:00-06:00">May 4, 1932—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>37. Referring to my telegram No. 35, May 1, 4 p.m., inauguration of Ricardo
                    Jiménez as President of Costa Rica will take place at noon, May 8th, and I
                    propose participating in inaugural ceremonies as <pb facs="0636" n="532"
                        xml:id="pg532"/> Dean of the Diplomatic Corps unless the Department cables
                    instructions to the contrary.</p>
                <p>No constitutional objections to right of Ricardo Jiménez to Presidency through
                    procedure by which he was chosen have come to my knowledge and I concur in the
                    general feeling that he is the only man for the post.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
